{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1233170-can-you-destroy-permanently-i-mean-a-mummy-s-body-by-having-it-eaten","id":1233170,"title":"can you destroy(permanently i mean) a mummy's body by having it eaten?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-08T05:05:58-07:00","id":1233170,"title":"can you destroy(permanently i mean) a mummy's body by having it eaten?","content":"let's say you go with the classic mafia option,shred it to bits and then feed it to pigs. most of it will be absorbed and eventually converted into energy(mostly heat and kinetic force i believe). at this point i assume that this part of the body is as irretrievable as it gets. Then you feet the excrement to animals (such as flies) that eat it. and so on until nothing is left that contains even an atom of something that used to have the mummy's dna on it.<br /> <br /> should this work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T14:29:33-07:00","id":1233271,"title":"","content":"The post-Reckoning ones, I don't know. But pre-Reckoning ones, I think it was specifically mentioned in the second edition that, yes, they will eventually come back, but it takes a long time. IIRC, this was cited as a main reason for not antagonizing Mokole by trespassing on their territories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T06:54:14-07:00","id":1233410,"title":"","content":"Post-Reckoning no. According to the book only something on the level of being at the center of a nuclear explosion could permanently destroy one (maybe).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T07:10:41-07:00","id":1233413,"title":"","content":"The post-Reckoning mummies would also return. While the body has been sundered quite effectively, there is still enough matter left for the khat to reform. Really, anything short of being at the center of a high-yield nuclear detonation won't stop the resurrection.<br /> <br /> Now, if you are running a non-mummy game and have a mummy antagonist that you want the characters to be able to defeat then, yes, your plan should work if it is best for the story. Just keep in mind that a mummy without a body is still a very powerful spiritual presence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T13:41:38-07:00","id":1233494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThomasM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1233170-can-you-destroy-permanently-i-mean-a-mummy-s-body-by-having-it-eaten?p=1233413#post1233413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The post-Reckoning mummies would also return. While the body has been sundered quite effectively, there is still enough matter left for the khat to reform. Really, anything short of being at the center of a high-yield nuclear detonation won't stop the resurrection.<br /> <br /> Now, if you are running a non-mummy game and have a mummy antagonist that you want the characters to be able to defeat then, yes, your plan should work if it is best for the story. Just keep in mind that a mummy without a body is still a very powerful spiritual presence.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> if a body is eaten and excreted.. and then the excrement is also eaten (such as by insects) and then you repeat.. well eventually you should reach a point where no molecules of the mummy's body remain. at least if i get my biology right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-10T00:56:32-07:00","id":1233636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1233170-can-you-destroy-permanently-i-mean-a-mummy-s-body-by-having-it-eaten?p=1233494#post1233494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> if a body is eaten and excreted.. and then the excrement is also eaten (such as by insects) and then you repeat.. well eventually you should reach a point where no molecules of the mummy's body remain. at least if i get my biology right.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean? Molecules are molecules. They don't stop existing just because they've been used to produce chemical energy.<br /> <br /> Sooner or later, that matter is going to be drawn back from wherever all its particles have ended up, and the mummy will reform.<br /> <br /> The only reason you'd even bother is to make it harder for a mummy to come back. For a mortal, that's a pretty good deal (though they'd get the same result just burning them to dust and scattering the dust). For immortals - like vampires, some mages, and other mummies - it's not worth the effort, since they can live long enough to regret it. The Followers of Set don't go to such lengths for that very reason; the time bought is negligible on vampiric time scales, the mummy comes back pissed off, and in the meantime you're dealing with their already pissed off Ka.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-10T18:07:22-07:00","id":1233866,"title":"","content":"It's possible there might be otherworldly things one could feed a mummy to that would do the trick, but I'd imagine any such would be much more dangerous to deal with than the mummy him- or herself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T06:50:26-07:00","id":1233980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1233170-can-you-destroy-permanently-i-mean-a-mummy-s-body-by-having-it-eaten?p=1233636#post1233636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean? Molecules are molecules. They don't stop existing just because they've been used to produce chemical energy.<br /> <br /> Sooner or later, that matter is going to be drawn back from wherever all its particles have ended up, and the mummy will reform.<br /> <br /> The only reason you'd even bother is to make it harder for a mummy to come back. For a mortal, that's a pretty good deal (though they'd get the same result just burning them to dust and scattering the dust). For immortals - like vampires, some mages, and other mummies - it's not worth the effort, since they can live long enough to regret it. The Followers of Set don't go to such lengths for that very reason; the time bought is negligible on vampiric time scales, the mummy comes back pissed off, and in the meantime you're dealing with their already pissed off Ka.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> well of course conservation of energy/mass applies but once a fat cell(for instance) is &quot;burned&quot; during activity, it becomes energy. which doesn't have atoms right? ok, maybe not all of it becomes energy(bodies aren't so efficient) but much of it does the rest being removed during respiration i believe as well as sweating/urination","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T07:45:05-07:00","id":1233994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1233170-can-you-destroy-permanently-i-mean-a-mummy-s-body-by-having-it-eaten?p=1233980#post1233980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> well of course conservation of energy/mass applies but once a fat cell(for instance) is &quot;burned&quot; during activity, it becomes energy. which doesn't have atoms right? ok, maybe not all of it becomes energy(bodies aren't so efficient) but much of it does the rest being removed during respiration i believe as well as sweating/urination</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know the energy comes from the rupture of the chemical bonds that tie together the atoms that compose a molecule. So, you will always have atoms. Stomachs aren't nuclear fission reactors.<br /> <br /> Then again, I'm not sure if that won't be enough: How much damage does the ground zero of a nuclear blast cause to the body?. I know it &quot;disappears&quot; and may leave a &quot;shadow&quot; on walls - but what does that mean to the molecules and atoms that compose the body?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-11-2018, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T10:51:20-07:00","id":1234047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1233170-can-you-destroy-permanently-i-mean-a-mummy-s-body-by-having-it-eaten?p=1233980#post1233980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> well of course conservation of energy/mass applies but once a fat cell(for instance) is &quot;burned&quot; during activity, it becomes energy. which doesn't have atoms right? ok, maybe not all of it becomes energy(bodies aren't so efficient) but much of it does the rest being removed during respiration i believe as well as sweating/urination</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that trying to reason out why an in-game fictional (magical) process works or doesn't work by applying real-world science is usually an invitation to a massive headache without a solution. The answer &quot;because... magic&quot; doesn't sit well with many but, truth be told, that's exactly what we're dealing with here. Osiris designed the Spell of Life to overcome any conceivable physical damage (and I'll argue that Osiris never conceived of nuclear weapons) so mummies will almost always reform no matter what you throw at them.<br /> <br /> Again, if you are the storyteller and you don't like this then it is your prerogative to change it at your table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T12:50:08-07:00","id":1234074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1233170-can-you-destroy-permanently-i-mean-a-mummy-s-body-by-having-it-eaten?p=1233994#post1233994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as I know the energy comes from the rupture of the chemical bonds that tie together the atoms that compose a molecule. So, you will always have atoms. Stomachs aren't nuclear fission reactors.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, precisely.<br /> <br /> When we say &quot;matter cannot be created or destroyed&quot;, we aren't fooling around. When we say that, we MEAN it. Atoms don't just stop existing because the potential energy contained in the bonds between them are let loose as a result of chemical processes. Those atoms still exist. They've just changed form.<br /> <br /> I'm not even sure a nuclear blast can actually disassemble atoms. Even if it can, they'll just be reduced to subatomic particles, and thus the problem is merely moved down another step.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T02:50:41-07:00","id":1234219,"title":"","content":"Bonus trivia:<br /> If you weight a (dry!) log, then burn it up and actually manage to catch all the smoke particles and ash that gets produced, you will find that if you weight the stuff again it will weight MORE than it has before the log was burnt. Mind blown.<br /> <br /> This is because, while the matter of the burnt log has lost an absolutely miniscule amount of mass due of energy loss (Matter AND contained energy determine final mass), the matter the log consisted of actually has gained a whole pile of oxygen molecules <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Because, y'know, you need air to burn stuff for a reason. The oxygen binds to the burning stuffs (resulting in crispy things and ash), kicking other molecules out (smoke), and the change of the molecular bonds releases contained energy (as heat).<br /> <br /> So, if you subtract this mass of added oxygen, you will find that the remaining weight of all the ash and smoke is like 99.9999999% of what the log originally was. And that's it. And none of it comes from actual destruction of matter, just changes of molecule composition.<br /> <br /> There *is* a way to convert matter to energy (and vice versa), but this normally does not happen in everyday events. The most famous rare event of course being the Big Bang where a ton of energy got converted into the pile of matter known as the Universe. But they also converted matter into energy and vice versa in particle accelerators at an atomic level.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> TL;DR: Matter is essentially a form of solid energy, both matter and classic energy contained in it determine final mass, and normally there is no conversion between matter and energy happening in any way in everyday events. Also, neither can be literally destroyed, period. E=mc\u00b2 is king.<br /> <br /> <br /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 07-12-2018, 06:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T04:31:43-07:00","id":1234242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1233170-can-you-destroy-permanently-i-mean-a-mummy-s-body-by-having-it-eaten?p=1234074#post1234074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not even sure a nuclear blast can actually disassemble atoms.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, no it can't...well, a nuclear blast is the RESULT of buhzillions of atom's nuclei disassembling at once, not a cause.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> The mixed pile of protons and neutrons of a very unstable atom nucleus, as those in certain radioactive materials like specific forms of Uranium and Plutonium - strong radioactivity pretty much is the definiton of matter having unstable nuclei - gets hit with a neutron, splits up into two smaller nuclei, and the neutrons that are left over from that shoot out and hit other already very unstable nuclei around, causing the same reaction there. This is the Critical Mass's chain reaction that causes the explosion, releasing a HUGE amount of previously bound energy as all those countless unstable nuclei split nearly at once.<br /> And even there, no matter gets technically destroyed, as far as I know. The pieces just get split up, and the resulting smaller nuclei collect neutrons over a long time to become stable again (i.e. non-radioactive for the everyday definition of that.).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 07-12-2018, 07:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T04:58:20-07:00","id":1234247,"title":"","content":"Also, final 'Ambrosia does armchair science!' post!<br /> <br /> <br /> If you really were to take matter and converted it into energy, 100% (which again, isn't happening in anything in the previous posts), that's where E=mc\u00b2 comes in. That formula pretty much tells you exactly how much energy (non-travelling) matter consists of. Not the energy that holds the matter or molecules together, but the energy the matter (theoretically) can be converted into. Reverse-big-bang style.<br /> <br /> And then, using E=mc\u00b2, you might realize that one gram of matter converted 100% into pure energy would result in the same amount of energy that was released during the Hiroshima explosion. One. Gram. 0.0353 ounces.<br /> <br /> Now weight yourself, and consider the mindblowing, insane amount of energy that got converted into the matter your body consists of, at the beginning of time. It is quite amazing and scary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 07-12-2018, 08:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T14:36:34-07:00","id":1234406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1233170-can-you-destroy-permanently-i-mean-a-mummy-s-body-by-having-it-eaten?p=1234074#post1234074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This, precisely.<br /> <br /> When we say &quot;matter cannot be created or destroyed&quot;, we aren't fooling around. When we say that, we MEAN it. Atoms don't just stop existing because the potential energy contained in the bonds between them are let loose as a result of chemical processes. Those atoms still exist. They've just changed form.<br /> <br /> I'm not even sure a nuclear blast can actually disassemble atoms. Even if it can, they'll just be reduced to subatomic particles, and thus the problem is merely moved down another step.</div> </div> </div> </div>if they are reduced to subatomic particles then it DOES destroy the mummy's body. correct me if i'm wrong but if something only has subatomic particles and no atoms then it is energy right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T14:54:50-07:00","id":1234412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1233170-can-you-destroy-permanently-i-mean-a-mummy-s-body-by-having-it-eaten?p=1234406#post1234406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if they are reduced to subatomic particles then it DOES destroy the mummy's body. correct me if i'm wrong but if something only has subatomic particles and no atoms then it is energy right?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they are particles. Particles are still matter. They still have mass, and that mass hasn't gone anywhere.<br /> <br /> All of which is a moot point, since the digestive processes of animals don't have the capacity to reduce atoms to subatomic particles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T16:13:15-07:00","id":1234434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1233170-can-you-destroy-permanently-i-mean-a-mummy-s-body-by-having-it-eaten?p=1234412#post1234412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of which is a moot point, since the digestive processes of animals don't have the capacity to reduce atoms to subatomic particles.</div> </div> </div> </div>You really need better animals if yours can't do a little bit of particle physics... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> @Topic<br /> I believe one of the sample ideas for &quot;this will take them a <i>long</i> time to come back from&quot; was throwing the mummy into an active volcano. Feeding them to pigs is cute by comparison.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T01:36:15-07:00","id":1234561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1233170-can-you-destroy-permanently-i-mean-a-mummy-s-body-by-having-it-eaten?p=1234412#post1234412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, they are particles. Particles are still matter. They still have mass, and that mass hasn't gone anywhere.<br /> <br /> All of which is a moot point, since the digestive processes of animals don't have the capacity to reduce atoms to subatomic particles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course what could be interesting, given the topic, is the fact that lots of your food's atoms and molecules become a literal part of your body....<br /> <br /> *Mummy chestburster sounds*<br /> <br /> I kid, and I bet this is going into way more details than the original devs intended :P I think it's safe to say that the mummy reforms out of the, ahem, waste of the animals, or whatever it decomposes into depending on where it's tossed, over a long time. Which is probably one of the least dignified ways of forcing a Mummy into resurrection..then again, rising from the soil can be poetic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 07-13-2018, 04:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T08:35:16-07:00","id":1234650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1233170-can-you-destroy-permanently-i-mean-a-mummy-s-body-by-having-it-eaten?p=1234406#post1234406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if they are reduced to subatomic particles then it DOES destroy the mummy's body. correct me if i'm wrong but if something only has subatomic particles and no atoms then it is energy right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is: If the Ground Zero of an atomic explosion, RAW, does obliterate the mummy's body to the point of no return AND an atomic explosion isn't enough to trully reduce the body to subatomic particles, then you don't need to reduce the mummy's body to subatomic particles to bring it to the point of no return. If in the text we're invited to make paralelisms with atomic bombs, then anything that causes the same amount of damage on the body as an atomic bomb would do.<br /> <br /> I would think that being inside an erupting volcano may qualify, since eruptions are several times stronger than nuclear explosions<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T09:20:21-07:00","id":1234667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1233170-can-you-destroy-permanently-i-mean-a-mummy-s-body-by-having-it-eaten?p=1234650#post1234650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would think that being inside an erupting volcano may qualify, since eruptions are several times stronger than nuclear explosions</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there is also a difference between an active volcano's tip spewing lava, and being at the center of the eruption way, way, waaaay down inside the earth. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ...random fun fact:<br /> Lava isn't even that hot. A candle flame's center is a bit hotter than the lava coming out of a volcano. So, what we can take from that is, flamethrower the mummy until ash remains and you're good to go for a while as well. I guess the difference is that inside a volcano, the mummy's remains are constantly on fire &gt;_&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T21:46:37-07:00","id":1237887,"title":"","content":"Hmm an amusing trick would be to feed the mummy to something, then if you're still worried transport the excrement off world preferably between planes of existence. See how long that would take for a reform to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T12:49:17-07:00","id":1239412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1233170-can-you-destroy-permanently-i-mean-a-mummy-s-body-by-having-it-eaten?p=1237887#post1237887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm an amusing trick would be to feed the mummy to something, then if you're still worried transport the excrement off world preferably between planes of existence. See how long that would take for a reform to happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>The largest portion or the one on the most convenient location to the Underworld would be the site of the resurrection. Not all the Khat's matter needs to be brought together, just a surviving portion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T20:03:15-07:00","id":1240299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1233170-can-you-destroy-permanently-i-mean-a-mummy-s-body-by-having-it-eaten?p=1233271#post1233271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The post-Reckoning ones, I don't know. But pre-Reckoning ones, I think it was specifically mentioned in the second edition that, yes, they will eventually come back, but it takes a long time. IIRC, this was cited as a main reason for not antagonizing Mokole by trespassing on their territories.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both Post and Pre reckoning this will only delay their return.<br /> <br /> I would point out there are ways to eat Mummies to permanent Death. Redcaps for instance seem tie their supernatural digestion to some sort of primordial abyss/oblivion, so if a Redcap ate a Mummy, its not going to the Redcap's poop... its gone. And if something like an Akuma or other Soul Eater full on Eats a Mummies souls it is gone. Atom Bombs destroying a mummies body atom by atom is powerful enough to brute force destroy their return but they are still spirits, and in the World of Darkness Unnaming is very similar to atomic disintegration. I forget how easy it is for Mages to full on destroy a mummy without emulating Atomic Blasts, but I think its pretty tough for them. Demons could potentially develop a power to eat a mummies soul, but the books don't really give it to us. Demons can eat other Demons Souls, and I would allow them to Hsien souls because they are so similar. But it takes Earthbound to develop lore to eat Mortal Souls, but I would allow another Lore or Ritual or some sort of hellish power to Eat a supernatural soul. Diablerie is named after the Demons in the War of Wrath Eating Angels after all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T07:44:34-07:00","id":1240429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forget how easy it is for Mages to full on destroy a mummy without emulating Atomic Blasts, but I think its pretty tough for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>As per Revised: Spirit 5 + Prime 5 to permanently kill a mummy. Erasing it's body and spirit.<br /> <br /> If you only want to erase the body beyond regeneration, Prime 5 it's enough. Not really easier than emulating an Atomic Blast (Forces 5), but arguably easier than turning a vampire into a lawnchair (Life 5 + Matter).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-30-2018, 10:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T01:57:09-07:00","id":1252462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1233170-can-you-destroy-permanently-i-mean-a-mummy-s-body-by-having-it-eaten?p=1240429#post1240429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As per Revised: Spirit 5 + Prime 5 to permanently kill a mummy. Erasing it's body and spirit.<br /> <br /> If you only want to erase the body beyond regeneration, Prime 5 it's enough. Not really easier than emulating an Atomic Blast (Forces 5), but arguably easier than turning a vampire into a lawnchair (Life 5 + Matter).</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I'd throw in some Entropy; spirit 5 can't destroy any spirit permanently on its own, since the conceptual side of it still exists, or because the spirit retreats somewhere (like the shadowlands). To destroy the spirit entirely you'd definitely need at least Entropy 4.<br /> <br /> So something to destroy the body fully (Life or Prime or Forces would do), and something to destroy the soul (Spirit and Entropy).<br /> <br /> Or you could do something much easier; get the mummy on your side using mind/spirit, or the offer of magickal assistance. Eradicating them feels like overkill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T08:10:13-07:00","id":1253064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1233170-can-you-destroy-permanently-i-mean-a-mummy-s-body-by-having-it-eaten?p=1252462#post1252462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally I'd throw in some Entropy; spirit 5 can't destroy any spirit permanently on its own, since the conceptual side of it still exists, or because the spirit retreats somewhere (like the shadowlands). To destroy the spirit entirely you'd definitely need at least Entropy 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mummy souls aren't backed by a concept the way spirits are: Spirits ARE a concept (in Mage, in Werewolf it's different, but you're implying a HDYDT rule) : The Spirit of Democracy exists because Democracy exists, to kill that spirit you would need to erase or resignify Democracy. This does allow for near immortality, but at the cost of being 100% defined by the concept. Mummies are individual beings (like any playable splat) - they aren't forced to follow Osiris agenda and personality or cease to exist. Good for them, but they don't have a &quot;conceptual side&quot; to regenerate them after they die, that's just the magic of their soul and souls can be erased with Spirit alone.<br /> <br /> Nitpick: Entropy 4 does nothing to concepts. That's Entropy 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-10-2018, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T08:16:36-07:00","id":1253065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1233170-can-you-destroy-permanently-i-mean-a-mummy-s-body-by-having-it-eaten?p=1253064#post1253064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mummy souls aren't backed by a concept the way spirits are: Spirits ARE a concept (in Mage, in Werewolf it's different, but you're implying a HDYDT rule) : The Spirit of Democracy exists because Democracy exists, to kill that spirit you would need to erase or resignify Democracy. This does allow for near immortality, but at the cost of being 100% defined by the concept. Mummies are individual beings (like any playable splat) - they aren't forced to follow Osiris agenda and personality or cease to exist. Good for them, but they don't have a &quot;conceptual side&quot; to regenerate them after they die, that's just the magic of their soul and souls can be erased with Spirit alone.<br /> <br /> Nitpick: Entropy 4 does nothing to concepts. That's Entropy 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes a lot of sense!<br /> <br /> But I thought that Entropy 4 could erode belief? That's it unwinding a concept isn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T08:43:39-07:00","id":1253078,"title":"","content":"Entropy 4 allows to erode living things (and in general affect patterns that are too &quot;life-like&quot; to be affected by Entropy 3, like vampires). Entropy 5 it's needed to erode ideas, toughts and other psychic or social constructs. As per M20 p.515, but any Basic should have that writteup in the Entropy section too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-04T15:07:49-07:00","id":1258949,"title":"","content":"If you want to destroy a Mummy through eating it you have to use the Anthropophagi power used by the Amkhat found in the M:TR core rulebook (p.203). Every time you eat part of a Mummy you live longer and can steal from them: every time you do so you can steal one Ability point or one Attribute point from the Mummy until it's lost almost all of them. While this is possible in theory, in practice this means that you'd have to kill a Mummy over and over again and munch on the good bits (eyes, hands, body, brain or heart) over and over again. Plus, you'd need to beat the Mummy again and again, avoid other Mummies and their servants and have enough time on your hands to sit out the wait until the Mummy gets back each time this happens, which can range anywhere from a day to a year or more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-04T17:09:47-07:00","id":1258971,"title":"","content":"My money is that: <br /> <br /> You CAN eat a mummy...but it Will eventually come Out....<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}